#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editor/IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
vendor
go/nl6/nl6
go/nl6/nl6.pid
go/nl6/startup.log
go/nl6-reconcile

# Release build artifacts
dist/

# Docs site build output and local toolchain artefacts (Docusaurus)
build/
.docusaurus/
node_modules/

# AI tools — working directories for AI/agent CLIs and spec-driven workflows.
# Session-private, never committed.

# OpenSpec working directory — spec-driven change proposals, archived
# changes, and capability specs are managed as a local workflow artifact,
# not as versioned project documentation.
openspec/

# BMad framework scratch output (explorations, review artifacts).
_bmad-output/
_bmad/

# Per-CLI harness working directories (hooks, settings, transcripts,
# locally-configured skills). Each AI CLI keeps session-private state
# here; never shared, never committed. AGENTS.md / GEMINI.md are NOT
# listed because those are committed symlinks to CLAUDE.md (single
# source of truth for project context).
.agent/
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/
.gemini/




# Scenario report captured from the running simulator. The loadtest runbooks
# tell operators to write it into the CWD (`curl .../report > report.json`,
# docs/reference/loadtest-runbooks.md), so it lands at the repo root and
# otherwise shows up in `git status` after every load test.
/report.json
/collector.csv

# Local compose-bootstrap fleet manifest (see the docker getting-started doc);
# per-machine state, never committed. Start from inventory/devices.example.json.
inventory/devices.json

# nl6#534 / nl6#559 / nl6#560 — do not let a live `-fuzz` run commit a crasher.
#
# The self-differential agreement assertions in
# go/nl6/snmp_parser_robustness_test.go fire on two OPEN parser defects
# (nl6#559 getPDUType's one-octet version assumption, nl6#560
# parseGetBulkParams' missing `< 0` guards), so every target that calls
# assertV2cParserAgreement fails within seconds of live fuzzing. Go writes that
# failing input to testdata/fuzz/<target>/, and committing it would fail an
# ordinary `go test` for a defect nl6#534 is not permitted to repair.
#
# Only the target directories with NO committed corpus are listed. Ignoring
# FuzzHandleSingleRequest/ or FuzzHandleGetBulk/ would silently swallow genuine
# corpus additions to the 248 and 205 entries already tracked there — for those
# two, delete a crasher by hand.
#
# REMOVE THIS BLOCK when nl6#559 and nl6#560 land.
go/nl6/testdata/fuzz/FuzzGetPDUType/
go/nl6/testdata/fuzz/FuzzParseIncomingRequest/
go/nl6/testdata/fuzz/FuzzParseAllOIDsFromRequest/
go/nl6/testdata/fuzz/FuzzParseGetBulkParams/
go/nl6/testdata/fuzz/FuzzHandleGetRequestVarbinds/
go/nl6/testdata/fuzz/FuzzIsSNMPv3Request/
go/nl6/testdata/fuzz/FuzzV2cRequestRoundTrip/
